{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Those who consecrate themselves.</b> That they consecrate themselves to go after idolatry:" "<b>המטהרים.</b> Missing the tav of the hitpa'el, and it is from the root ב–ט–ה, with assimilation of the tav." "<b>אל הגנות.</b> Like the Asherot:" "<b>אחר אחת.</b> A single asherah, and it is written אחד and behold it is a tree, for every asherah is a tree:" "And the meaning of <b>בתוך</b> is that they were surrounding the asherah from this side and from that side, and so they are within, or within the garden:" "And <b>eaters of the flesh of the pig</b>: the meaning is that they consecrate it, while their bodies are full of impurity:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 66, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:01:17.730721117Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}